PAGE404: Breaking Tenant Isolation Through Hardware-assisted Page Migration
===========================================================================

This repository contains the artifact for PAGE404, to appear in the
proceedings of IEEE Security and Privacy 2027. The work studies how
hardware-assisted page migration on the NVIDIA GH200 (Hopper) leaks across
MIG tenant boundaries, and was responsibly disclosed to NVIDIA.

These are research proof-of-concept artifacts for a specific lab setup, not
deployable or general-purpose attacks.

Repository layout
-----------------
  page404_covert_channel/   Eviction-based covert channel between two MIG
                            slices (sender + receiver). See its README.md.

  page404_side_channel/     Migration-delay side channels: a shared CUDA
                            collector plus two PoCs —
                              prompt_length_estimate/  victim prompt-length estimation
                              llm_fingerprinting/       victim model fingerprinting
                            See page404_side_channel/README.md.

  page404_re/               Reverse-engineering of the page-migration behaviour.

  modified_page404_driver/  Modified NVIDIA GPU kernel driver used in the reevrse engineering study.

Getting started
---------------
Each component is self-contained and has its own build/run instructions in the
READMEs linked above. Target hardware is the NVIDIA GH200 with MIG enabled;
build scripts assume the CUDA toolkit and nvcc are on PATH.